#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1365 expect=noViolation domain=SUPPAE
#note "PERMANENT PIN OF A RULED DEVIATION - not a flip candidate (M2-P8, option (B), ruled 2026-08-21). The Check gates on RDOMAIN='DM', so the same population-flag QNAM attached to a non-DM parent is deliberately NOT reported. The PMDA sheet row 375 and the FDA sheet row 378 both say SUPPQUAL, but the ORIGINATING authority - CDISC CG0528, which the FDA row names as this rule's publisher (rows 1167-1168 of SDTM_and_SDTMIG_Conformance_Rules_v2.0) - says Domain: DM and writes 'ADSL Population flags not in SUPPDM' into its Rule cell. coreJ follows CDISC; the PMDA/FDA SUPPQUAL cells read as the class name for supplemental qualifiers rather than as a domain list. The deviation is on the record as a PMDA sheet issue under M2-D31 (owed by the ruling, filed by the coordinator). ⛔ Do NOT re-aim this fixture to expect=violation: doing so would implement option (A), which was REJECTED. Twin: fda/FDA-SD1365/FDA-SD1365-valid_other_rdomain-SUPPAE.cdt, identical pin."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset SUPPAE label="Supplemental Qualifiers for AE"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | AESEQ | 1 | SAFFL | Safety Population Flag | Y
